  "worked_solution": "We have $\\frac{4}{5}$ on the left and $\\frac{8}{15}$ on the right.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14130839/assets/42e28264486cfa85290de0bad34ea6e0121fe77c00bc36003fedbca4ebcb1f46.png)\n\nThe shape on the right-hand side is split into $3$ equal parts by horizontal lines.\nSo, the shaded part on the right is $\\frac{2}{3}$ of the shaded part on the left. \n\nTherefore, the multiplication problem shown is\n\n$$\n\\frac{4}{5}\\times \\frac{2}{3}=\\frac{8}{15}.\n$$\n\nSo, the missing number is $2.$",
